  "markdown": "<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">FACE OF CURB FINISHED GRADE 5\" SEE NOTE 1 NYSDOT TYPE (NVF) 16\" 8\" 4\" 6\" TYP PLACE CONCRETE BACKING TO BOTTOM OF BASE COURSE CONCRETE BACKING 3500 PSI DRY MIX CONCRETE CONTINUOUS BED COMPACTED SUBGRADE \n\n<description>Cross-section detail of a curb foundation. A vertical hatched concrete curb stem, 5 inches wide, rises from a horizontal dry mix concrete continuous bed 4 inches thick, which sits on compacted subgrade shown with crosshatched earth pattern. The top of the curb aligns with a horizontal line labeled FINISHED GRADE, and the curb face is labeled FACE OF CURB with a vertical reference line. A dimension of 16 inches runs from finished grade down to the bed. On the right side, a concrete backing with stippled fill and triangular aggregate marks, labeled CONCRETE BACKING 3500 PSI, has an 8 inch height and a chamfered top edge sloping down toward the right; its base width is 6 inches typical. On the left, the concrete backing fills to the bottom of the base course, shown as stacked layers of asphalt-like and base course hatching, with a dimension labeled SEE NOTE 1 measured from the finished grade line to the top of the base course.</description></figure>\n\n<u>NOTES:</u>\n\n1. FOR NEW CONSTRUCTION, A 6\" CURB REVEAL SHALL BE MAINTAINED. MATCH EXISTING REVEAL FOR CURB REPLACEMENT OR RESETTING.\n\nNO SCALE |\n\n[logo: ALBANY NEW YORK | EST. 1686]\n\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E. City Engineer\n\n<table>\n<tr><td>CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL NAME:<br>GRANITE CURB INSTALLATION DETAIL</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<table>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No.<br>C-1</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>C-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/26/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">2'-0\" WEDGE CURB\nFINISHED GRADE (TYP)\n1-1/2\" TOP COURSE\n4\"\n12\"\nTACK COAT (TYP)\nASPHALT CONCRETE TOP COURSE\nASPHALT BASE COURSE\nSUBBASE COURSE\n\n\n<description>Cross-section diagram of a pavement edge with a wedge curb. A horizontal layered structure extends from left to right, with a subbase course at the bottom shown as a large stippled rectangle, an asphalt base course above it shown with diagonal hatching, and a thin 1-1/2\" top course at the left. A dimension line labeled 2'-0\" WEDGE CURB spans the top of a tapered asphalt concrete top course (stippled wedge) that rises from the top course surface to the curb face at the right. At the right edge, a 4\" dimension is marked from the finished grade line down to the base level, with a hatched curb section and a finished grade line sloping upward to the right, labeled FINISHED GRADE (TYP). A 12\" horizontal dimension is shown along the bottom right of the base layer. A thin tack coat layer (TYP) is indicated between the asphalt layers. Leader lines point to each labeled layer.</description></figure>\n\n# NOTES:\n\n1. MAINTAIN EXISTING TRAVEL LANE(S) WIDTH PER TRAFFIC ENGINEERING.\n\nNO SCALE\n\n[logo: ALBANY NEW YORK | EST. 1686]\n\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>ASPHALT WEDGE CURB DETAIL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No. C-2</td><td>FILE NAME: C-2.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/26/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">ADA DETECTABLE WARNING REFER TO CR-2 AND NYSDOT 608-01 STANDARD SHEETS FOR PLACEMENT AND CONFIGURATION\nBROOM FINISH (TYP)\nCURB\n5'-0\"\n5'-0\"\n5'-0\"\n\n\n<description>Line drawing of a curved curb-ramp plan showing three adjacent sloped ramp segments running along a curved curb line at the lower left, each labeled with a black wedge-shaped slope arrow marked 1:12 (the left and right segments show the 1 and 12 labels, the center segment shows 12 with 1 at its base). The left and right segments are hatched with fine parallel broom-finish lines, and the center segment is filled with a field of small oval/circle detectable-warning dots. Each segment is bounded by double-line edges, and dimension lines beneath the curb indicate each segment is 5'-0\" wide along the curb. A leader line points from the ADA detectable warning note to the dotted center segment, and another leader line points from the BROOM FINISH (TYP) note to a hatched segment. Curb is labeled with a leader arrow at the upper left.</description></figure>\n\n<u>NOTE:</u>\n\n1. CURB SHALL BE FLUSH WITH PAVEMENT AT ROADWAY.\n\n2. SEE STANDARD DETAILS FOR CURB AND SIDEWALK INSTALLATION.\n\n3. SEE STANDARD DETAIL FOR ADA DETECTABLE WARNING STRIP INSTALLATION.\n\n4. INSTALLATION SHALL MEET ALL APPLICABLE ADA CODES AND STANDARDS.\n\n5. REFER TO NYSDOT 608-01 STANDARD SHEETS FOR APPLICABLE CURB RAMP LAYOUT FOR EACH INDIVIDUAL CURB RAMP\n\n[logo: ALBANY NEW YORK | EST. 1686]\n\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n<table>\n<tr><td>CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL NAME:<br>ADA CURB RAMP DETAIL</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<table>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No. <br>CR-1</td><td>FILE NAME: <br>CR-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED <br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE <br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\nNO SCALE |\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">CAST IN PLACE DETECTABLE WARNING SURFACE TILE BY ARMOR TILE OR APPROVED EQUAL\nREMAINING PORTION OF RAMP TO RECEIVE BROOM FINISH IN ACCORDANCE WITH ADA STANDARDS\nWARNING STRIP SHALL EXTEND OVER FULL WIDTH OF RAMP (5'-0\" MIN)\nA\nA\n2'-0\" MIN\nPLAN\n\n\n<description>Plan view of a rectangular ramp outlined by a thin border. The upper large portion of the ramp is filled with evenly spaced horizontal broom-finish lines, labeled with a leader arrow stating the remaining portion of ramp receives broom finish per ADA standards. The lower portion, about 2'-0\" minimum deep and spanning the full ramp width, is filled with a regular grid of small open circles representing the cast-in-place detectable warning surface tile, with a leader labeled with the Armor Tile reference. A dimension line along the bottom spans the full ramp width labeled warning strip shall extend over full width of ramp (5'-0\" min). Section cut markers labeled A are shown on the left and right sides at the level of the warning strip. A vertical dimension on the right indicates the 2'-0\" minimum depth of the warning strip. The title PLAN is centered below the drawing.</description></figure>\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">PLAN\n\n\n<description>Cross-sectional construction detail drawn in black line work showing a cast-in-place detectable warning tile installation. A rectangular detectable warning tile block sits on top, with a row of semicircular dome bumps along its top surface. A leader line from the label \"CAST IN PLACE DETECTABLE WARNING TILE NYSDOT ITEM 608.21\" points to the top of the tile. Below the tile is a wider rectangular 4\" concrete slab, shown with stippled and aggregate hatching. Beneath it is a dashed horizontal line representing the grade or subgrade, with a 6\" MIN. CRUSHED STONE base layer of stippled fill extending down and out to both sides. A leader from \"4\" CONCRETE\" points to the concrete slab. A leader from \"6\" MIN. CRUSHED STONE\" points to the stone base on the left. On both left and right ends, sloped sidewalk or pavement edges with stippled fill and small X-marked anchor or joint symbols connect to the tile block. At the far right, a hatched earth or soil symbol sits at the subgrade line.</description></figure>\n\n<u>NOTES:</u>\n\n1. THE COLOR OF THE DETECTABLE WARNING SURFACE SHALL BE DARK GRAY, MUNSELL BOOK NOTATION BG-PB 3/5. THIS COLOR IS THE CITY OF ALBANY STANDARD COLOR FOR DETECTABLE WARNING SURFACES.\n\n2. SEE STANDARD DETAILS FOR CURB, SIDEWALK, AND SIDEWALK RAMP INSTALLATION.\n\n3. INSTALLATION SHALL MEET ALL APPLICABLE ADA CODES AND STANDARDS.\n\nNO SCALE\n\n[logo: ALBANY NEW YORK | EST. 1686]\n\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>ADA DETECTABLE WARNING STRIP DETAIL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No. CR-2</td><td>FILE NAME: CR-2.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED 09/16/03</td><td>REVISION DATE 03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n# SECTION A—A\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">NEW OR EXISTING DRIVEWAY; 6\" CONCRETE (SEE DETAIL SW-1); MAX. GRADIENT 1:12 (AND 1:50 CROSS-SLOPE IF WITHIN WALKING PATH); MATCH EXISTING GRADE (TYP); BROOM FINISH (TYP); CONCRETE SIDEWALK; MATCH EXISTING; GRANITE CURBING; 6'-0\"; VARIES, MATCH EXISTING DRIVEWAY WIDTH; PAVED ROADWAY\n\n\n<description>Isometric construction detail of a curb-cut driveway ramp connecting a paved roadway at the lower left-front to a concrete sidewalk at the upper right. The ramp surface is divided into hatched broom-finished concrete panels separated by thin joint lines, with stippled areas on the flanking sidewalk and ramp returns. Leader lines point to the new or existing driveway, 6-inch concrete thickness with reference to detail SW-1, maximum gradient 1:12 with 1:50 cross-slope note for walking path, matched existing grade, broom finish, granite curbing on the side edges, and a 6'-0\" dimension across the panel depth. A bracketed dimension labeled varies, match existing driveway width runs along the front edge of the ramp.</description></figure>\n\n<u>NOTE:</u>\n\n1. CURB REVEALS SHALL BE 1/2\" MAX WHERE RAMP MEETS PAVEMENT AT ROADWAY.\n\n2. SIDEWALK SHALL BE INSTALLED FLUSH WITH EXISTING DRIVEWAY.\n\n3. SEE STANDARD SIDEWALK DETAIL FOR SIDEWALK INSTALLATION.\n\nNO SCALE\n\n[logo: ALBANY NEW YORK | EST. 1686]\n\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>DRIVEWAY/SIDEWALK DROP CURB</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No.<br>DW-1</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>DW-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">EXISTING ASPHALT PAVEMENT (TYP)\n18\" LIMITS OF DISTURBANCE 18\"\nSAWCUT PAVEMENT (TYP)\n2\" THICK ASPHALT PAVEMENT TOP COURSE (9.5MM OR 6.5 MM AGGREGATE)\nTACK COAT (TYP.)\n8\" CONCRETE FOUNDATION FOR PAVEMENT\n12\" SUBBASE COURSE\nEXCAVATION LIMITS\nTRENCH BACKFILL, BACKFILL IN 6\" LIFTS, COMPACT PER SPECIFICATIONS\n\n\n<description>Cross-section construction detail of a pavement trench repair. At the top, a horizontal existing asphalt pavement layer spans the width, labeled on the left with a leader line. Below it, a centered band marked by dimension arrows labeled 18\" on the left, LIMITS OF DISTURBANCE across the middle, and 18\" on the right, indicating the repair zone. The top layer is a hatched 2\" asphalt top course with a sawcut edge at both ends (SAWCUT PAVEMENT (TYP)). Beneath it is an 8\" concrete foundation layer with triangular aggregate pattern, and below that a 12\" subbase course with dotted stipple fill. A thin tack coat line sits at the interface of the asphalt and existing pavement at the left. The excavated trench is shown below the pavement with hatched brick-like excavation limits on both sides, and the trench interior is labeled as trench backfill compacted in 6\" lifts per specifications.</description></figure>\n\n**NOTE:**\n\n1. IF LIMITS OF TRENCHING EXCEEDS 50 FEET, CONTRACTOR SHALL COMPLETE CURB TO CURB MILLING PER CITY DETAIL SR-3; UNLESS OTHERWISE ORDERED BY CITY OF ALBANY DEPARTMENT OF GENERAL SERVICES.\n\n2. ALL PAVEMENT MARKINGS DISTURBED SHALL BE RESTORED TO THE SATISFACTION OF THE CITY OF ALBANY DIVISION OF TRAFFIC ENGINEERING.\n\n3. ALL JOINTS TO BE SEALED WITH ASPHALT EMULSION (AC-20)\n\n4. ASHPHALT, CONCRETE TACK COAT, TRENCH BACKFILL AND OTHER MATERIALS AND OPERATIONS SHALL CONFORM TO NYSDOT STANDARDS AND SPECIFICATIONS UNLESS NOTED OR DIRECTED OTHERWISE BY THE CITY.\n\nNO SCALE\n\n<table>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"3\">ALBANY<br>NEW YORK | EST. 1686<br>Katherine M. Sheehan, Mayor<br>Howard M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer</td><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>STREET RESTORATION DETAIL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No. SR-1</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>SR-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">EXISTING ASPHALT PAVEMENT (TYP) SEAL ALL JOINTS SAWCUT PAVEMENT (TYP) 18\" LIMITS OF DISTURBANCE 18\" 10\" TEMPORARY 2500 PSI CONCRETE MILL CONCRETE AND REPLACE WITH 2\" ASPHALT TOP COURSE AFTER WINTER TIME PERIOD 12\" SUBBASE COURSE COMPACT IN 6\" LIFTS EXCAVATION LIMITS TRENCH BACKFILL, BACKFILL IN 6\" LIFTS, COMPACT PER SPECIFICATIONS \n\n<description>Cross-section construction detail of a pavement trench repair. A horizontal existing asphalt pavement surface runs across the top, with a sawcut pavement edge marked at both sides of a rectangular repair block. The top layer is a hatched 10\" temporary 2500 PSI concrete slab spanning the full width, with an 18\" dimension on each side outside a central LIMITS OF DISTURBANCE dimension. Below it, a stippled 12\" subbase course fills the rectangular block, flanked by hatched existing ground on both sides. A dashed excavation limit outline extends downward beneath the block, forming a U-shaped trench with trench backfill noted inside it. Leader lines point to each layer and joint, including SEAL ALL JOINTS at the right sawcut edge.</description></figure>\n\n<u>NOTES:</u>\n\n1. CONTRACTOR SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR MAINTAINING TEMPORARY WEARING SURFACE UNTIL PERMANENT PAVEMENT IS IN PLACE. TEMPORARY CONCRETE WEARING SURFACE SHALL BE REMOVED AND PERMANENT PAVEMENT RESTORATION COMPLETED NO LATER THAN MAY 15. PERMANENT PAVEMENT RESTORATION SHALL BE INSTALLED IN ACCORDANCE WITH CITY STANDARD DETAILS AND TO THE SATISFACTION OF THE CITY OF ALBANY.\n\n2. ALL JOINTS TO BE SEALED WITH ASPHALT EMULSION (AC-20)\n\n3. ALL WORK SHALL BE INSPECTED AND APPROVED BY THE CITY. NO SCALE\n\n[logo: ALBANY NEW YORK | EST. 1686]\n\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>STREET RESTORATION — WINTER CONDITIONS<br>NOVEMBER 1 — APRIL 15</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No.<br>SR-2</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>SR-2.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">LIMITS OF ROADWAY\nMILL A MINIMUM OF 2\" OF EXISTING TOP COURSE FROM ROADWAY\nLIMITS OF TRENCH EXCAVATION. REFER TO DETAIL SR-1 FOR FULL DEPTH PAVING RESTORATION REQUIREMENTS\nTACK COAT\n2\" ASPHALT CONCRETE TOP COURSE\nNOTE:\n1. PAVEMENT MILLING OPERATION SHALL EXTEND 5 FEET BEYOND THE LIMITS OF TRENCHING OR AS ORDERED BY THE ENGINEER.\n2. ALL JOINTS TO BE SEALED WITH ASPHALT EMULSION (AC-20)\nNO SCALE\n\n\n<description>Cross-sectional engineering detail of a roadway pavement restoration. A dimension line spanning the top labeled LIMITS OF ROADWAY runs between two vertical boundary lines. The roadway surface is a thin hatched band of asphalt, peaked near the center and sloping down toward both edges, bounded on each side by vertical lines representing curbs or adjacent pavement. A dashed outline beneath the surface shows a trench excavation, with a tack coat line along its upper edge. Leader lines point to the hatched 2-inch asphalt concrete top course, the tack coat, the trench limits, and a dimension arrow indicating the milled depth of 2 inches of existing top course. The drawing is in black line work on a white background with no scale.</description></figure>\n\n[logo: ALBANY NEW YORK | EST. 1686]\n\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>PAVEMENT MILLING AND<br>STREET RESTORATION<br>(REQUIRED LIMITS OF WORK ARE CURB TO CURB)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No. SR-3</td><td>FILE NAME: SR-3.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED 05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE 03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">18\" MIN LIMITS OF DISTURBANCE 18\" MIN RESET PAVERS IN MORTAR SETTING BED, 6\"± TOTAL DEPTH, MORTAR PAVER JOINTS WITH NON SHRINK GROUT 8\" CONCRETE FOUNDATION CLASS \"C\" CONCRETE WIRE FABRIC FOR CONCRETE REINFORCEMENT, NYSDOT SPECIFICATION 12\" SUBBASE COURSE TRENCH BACKFILL, BACKFILL IN 6\" LIFTS, COMPACT PER SPECIFICATIONS EXCAVATION LIMITS EXISTING PAVERS (TYP)\n\n\n<description>Cross-section detail of a paver restoration. A row of rectangular pavers runs across the top, with the central section labeled LIMITS OF DISTURBANCE and 18\" MIN dimension lines marked on each side. Below the pavers is a mortar setting bed, then a horizontal wire fabric reinforcement layer, then an 8\" concrete foundation layer, and a 12\" subbase course at the bottom. Existing pavers sit at the outer edges with hatched soil on both sides. A dashed excavation limits line encloses the trench beneath the disturbed area, with trench backfill noted within it. Leader lines connect each label to the corresponding layer or boundary.</description></figure>\n\n<u>NOTE:</u>\n\n1. HISTORIC DISTRICT LIMITS:\n\n   MADISON AVENUE: LARK STREET TO THE HUDSON RIVER\nLARK STREET: MADISON AVENUE TO CLINTON AVENUE\nCLINTON AVENUE: LARK STREET TO HUDSON RIVER\n\n2. CONTRACTOR SHALL NOTIFY CITY ENGINEER'S OFFICE 72 HOURS PRIOR TO COMMENCING RESTORATION FOR INSPECTION OF THE RESTORATION.\n\n3. ALL WORK SHALL BE COMPLETED TO THE SATISFACTION OF THE CITY.    NO SCALE\n\n[logo: ALBANY NEW YORK | EST. 1686]\n\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>STREET RESTORATION — GRANITE/BRICK PAVEMENT WITHIN HISTORIC DISTRICT (EXPOSED COBBLES)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No.<br>SR-4</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>SR-4.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>03/21/04</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">6\" FOR DRIVEWAYS AND TRAFFIC AREAS\n4\" FOR ALL OTHER AREAS\nPANEL LAYOUT AOBE\nPREMOLDED BITUMINOUS EXPANSION JOINT FILLER W/ SEALANT AT 20' O.C.\n6\"x6\"xW4xW4 REINFORCING MESH AT MID DEPTH\n6\" MIN. CRUSHED STONE, TYPE 2\n\n\n<description>Cross-sectional construction detail of a concrete slab shown in side elevation. The slab is drawn as a horizontal rectangular band with a thin solid top and bottom outline, containing a horizontal reinforcing mesh line at mid depth marked with small X symbols and scattered aggregate stipple dots. A vertical dimension arrow on the far left, labeled with the thickness notes, points to the slab top and bottom edges. A horizontal dimension line above the slab spans the panel layout length, labeled PANEL LAYOUT AOBE, with vertical tick ends at both sides. At the right end of the panel, a hatched vertical rounded block represents the premolded bituminous expansion joint filler with sealant, with a leader line pointing to it from the upper right text. Below the slab, a dashed line represents the crushed stone base, with stippled dots indicating the stone layer, and a leader from the lower left points to it. At lower right, diagonal hatching represents the compacted subgrade soil beneath the slab. Thin vertical slab-joint lines separate adjacent panels, and a small upward arrow at the lower left of the slab indicates the slab depth dimension.</description></figure>\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"3\">DESIGN ELEMENT TOLERANCES</td></tr>\n<tr><td>ELEMENT</td><td>DESIGN AND FIELD LAYOUT LIMIT</td><td>LIMIT FOR WORK ACCEPTANCE</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SIDEWALK CROSS SLOPE</td><td>1.5% MAX.</td><td>2.0% MAX.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SIDEWALK GRADE (RUNNING SLOPE)</td><td>4.5% MAX.</td><td>5.0% MAX.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CURB RAMP GRADE (RUNNING SLOPE)</td><td>7.5% MAX.</td><td>8.3% MAX.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>BLENDED TRANSITION GRADE (RUNNING SLOPE)</td><td>4.5% MAX.</td><td>5.0% MAX.</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<u>NOTE:</u> REFER TO NYSDOT STANDARD SHEETS 608-01.\n\n__NOTES:__\n\n1. THE CONCRETE USED SHALL BE PORTLAND CEMENT, AIR-ENTRAINED, CLASS \"A\" CONCRETE WITH AN AIR CONTENT OF 5%, MIN., TO 7%, MAX., AND A SLUMP OF THREE INCHES, MIN., TO FIVE INCHES, MAX. NO FLY ASH AND MIN. 4,000 PSI.\n\n2. ALL SIDEWALKS SHALL BE FINISHED WITH A BROOM FINISH UNLESS DIRECTED OTHERWISE BY THE CITY.\n\n3. EXPANSION JOINTS TO BE PLACED BETWEEN ADJACENT SLABS, AT BUILDING LINE, AT CURBS, OR AT PENETRATING STRUCTURES.\n\n4. SIDEWALKS SHALL BE INSTALLED WITH A MAXIMUM CROSS SLOPE OF 2.0%\n\n5. ALL SIDEWALKS PANEL REPLACEMENT SHALL BE UP TO THE NEAREST SIDEWALK JOINT. NO PARTIAL PANEL REPLACEMENT IS ALLOWED\n\nNO SCALE\n\n<table>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"2\">[image: Albany New York city logo with orange ornaments] ALBANY NEW YORK | EST. 1686</td><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>SIDEWALK INSTALLATION DETAIL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Katherine M. Sheehan, Mayor<br>Howard M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer</td><td>DETAIL No.<br>SW-1</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>SW-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">NOTE:\n\n\n<description>Technical engineering diagram of a crosswalk with curb ramp. A horizontal crosswalk band runs left to right with two thick black horizontal stripe borders (top and bottom) and multiple thick black vertical stripes spaced across it, forming white reflectorized pavement stripes between them. Dimension labels: \"6\"\" at top-left indicating stripe border thickness with a small arrow, \"8' MIN. PER CITY OF ALBANY TRAFFIC ENGINEERING\" written vertically on the left with a dimension line spanning the crosswalk width, \"12\"\" and \"36\"\" dimension arrows at bottom-left indicating stripe width and spacing. A leader arrow labeled \"WHITE EPOXY REFLECTORIZED PAVEMENT STRIPES\" points to the lower stripe border. On the right, a stippled concrete ramp shape with a curved curb line labeled \"CURB LINE\" at upper right; the ramp is labeled \"RAMP\" with a leader arrow, and it has chamfered corners tapering to the curb on the right side. Two vertical solid lines bound the left edge of the crosswalk and the right edge of the curb area.</description></figure>\n\n__NOTE:__\n\n1. EPOXY TO COMPLY WITH NYSDOT STANDARDS\n\n2. MUTCD MANUAL, SECTION 3B SHALL BE USED PER CITY OF ALBANY\nTRAFFIC ENGINEERING RECOMMENDATIONS.\n\nNO SCALE\n\n[logo: ALBANY NEW YORK | EST. 1686]\n\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY — DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>CROSSWALK DETAIL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No. CW-1</td><td>FILE NAME: CW-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED 12/9/03</td><td>REVISION DATE 03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- doc_id=parse-01m7rvy0c1mb6hxnedzemww2k7 -->",
